            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on the glass and frame, so check the listed weight of the specific door. As a guide, glass suppliers put quarter-inch glass at about three pounds per square foot, so a 36 by 84 inch door with mostly glass could carry 50 to 60 pounds of glass before the frame is added. Choose hardware rated comfortably above the total."
          }
