            "text": "Add two to three inches of overlap on each side of the opening, then split the total between two doors. A 60 inch opening needs about 64 inches of coverage, or two doors of roughly 32 inches. The track needs to be about twice the total coverage so both doors can clear the opening, and each side needs clear wall at least one door wide."
