        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A French barn door is the right choice when you want light and floor space more than you want privacy or quiet. It suits home offices for solo work, pantries, dens and wide openings between living spaces, and it suits them very well. It does not suit rooms that need a latching, sealed door, and no glass choice changes that.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Before you buy, check four things: the glass type for the room's evening use, clear wall on the side or sides the door slides to, solid framing behind the track, and hardware rated well above the door's real weight. Get those right and the door will glide quietly for years.
          </p>
        </div>

